    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)` and reworked the household/duplicate semantics in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` to match the new spec.\n\n**Core changes** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n1. **Deterministic `householdId`** \u2014 replaced the old `(lastName, address)` hash (formatted `HH-<HEX12>`) with the first 12 hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, reusing the existing `sha256HexPrefix` helper. The last name is normalized case-insensitively (trim + lowercase), and an absent postcode contributes the empty string. Owners with the same last name + postcode now derive the same id automatically. Removed the now-unused `normalizeForHousehold` helper.\n\n2. **`sharesHousehold` only bypasses the block** \u2014 in `addOwner`, the household id is now *always* computed (no longer conditional on `sharesHousehold`), so duplicate detection, `householdSize`, and the identity key all key off the real computed id.\n\n3. **New household-duplicate rejection** \u2014 added `rejectDuplicateHousehold(householdId, sharesHousehold)`: if another owner already carries the same computed `householdId` and the request did **not** set `sharesHousehold`, it throws `DuplicateHouseholdException` (\u2192 409). Setting `sharesHousehold` bypasses this so the owner is created as a declared member.\n\n4. **Declared members aren't flagged** \u2014 `possibleDuplicateOf` is now `null` when `sharesHousehold` is true, so a declared household member is never marked a possible duplicate.\n\nI also refreshed the now-stale docs (`householdSize` javadoc, `DuplicateHouseholdException` javadoc, and the OpenAPI `householdId`/`sharesHousehold`/`identityKey` descriptions and examples) to describe postcode-based keying.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` acceptance test passes (same lastName+postcode share the id via `sharesHousehold`; a different lastName yields a different id).",
